WEBVTT

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.351
EP: No, no, because listen to this,

00:10:01.375 --> 00:10:04.143
it was a moment like you all have,

00:10:04.167 --> 00:10:05.893
you have moments like that too.

00:10:05.917 --> 00:10:08.893
That's like a paradigmatic shift, right?

00:10:08.917 --> 00:10:10.184
I'm in training.

00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:12.643
This is many years back,
but it stayed with me,

00:10:12.667 --> 00:10:14.809
like the vista opened up

00:10:14.833 --> 00:10:17.750
and I was working
with families with depression.

00:10:19.958 --> 00:10:22.518
And at one point my teacher says

00:10:22.542 --> 00:10:24.417
that the depressed has all the power.

00:10:25.654 --> 00:10:27.893
And I thought -- this is
a moment where you stop

00:10:27.917 --> 00:10:30.632
because I'm thinking you're anhedonic,
you feel powerless,